id: decisions/046-proof-a-reader-can-open
title: "A proof source a reader can actually open"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'source-reachability'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: source-reachability
axis_gloss: "whether a cited source can be opened by anyone reading the record, or only by its author on their own machine"
poles:
  a: independently-reachable-source
  b: author-only-source
split: leaning
draft_status: full
leverage: 4.2
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(6) x split_weight(0.7) x authored_conflict_bonus(1)"

question: >
  May a record call itself source-backed when its source is a file only Dave can
  open, and may an automation contract name Dave's private machine as its
  workspace without saying so?

why_it_matters: >
  yawn.yawn promises orientation that is inspectable and replayable, yet two
  references claim source-backed on Windows user-profile paths, four of five scheduled
  bots run against a workspace root no reader can reach, and the loop contract
  hardcodes an operator's email; the in-flight proof-refs validator already
  freezes the two proof cases by name. Once answered, a bot writing a receipt
  knows whether a private path earns 'source-backed' or only 'reported', and a
  child Yawn on another machine knows which contracts it can run at all.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    4 judgments sit at independently-reachable-source (0 authored) and 2 at
    author-only-source (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions on
    this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether the two Desktop and Downloads sources can be published at all, and
    whether the notification email in core-loop.yawn is meant to be public.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Every proof.source, and every workspace, source_repo or memory root
      named by an active automation contract, resolves inside the repository or to a
      public URL. A private source is vendored with private material removed, or the
      claim it backs is relabelled reported or asserted-unverified.
      Operator-specific paths and emails move to an untracked local config the
      contract names by key.
    cost: "Vendoring or relabelling two references; rewriting workspace: in six active records to a config key; a local config mechanism the repo does not have yet."
    risk: "The real operational root disappears from the tree and the automations become harder, not easier, to inspect."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs (in-flight) already rejects new external proof sources; extend it to scan workspace:, source_repo: and canonical_memory.root: in automation/*.yawn and core-loop.yawn for drive-letter paths with no grandfather set; today six files fail."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0196"
      - "J0353"
      - "J0710"
      - "J1224"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: A source on the author's machine is an acceptable proof source and earns
      source-backed; the record notes that only the author can open it.
    cost: "Contradicts the test-enforced index reachability rule for governance records and the canonical_sentence's 'inspectable'."
    risk: "Any claim becomes source-backed by naming a file nobody else can check, which is worse than no proof."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None can enforce this; the record would be removing the external-source rejection from validate-proof-refs."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0708"
      - "J0782"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: A proof: block must be reachable from the tree or a public URL (already
      enforced, two records grandfathered by name with a ceiling of two that may
      only shrink), and a grandfathered record may carry proof.status: reported or
      source-backed-private, never source-backed. An operational contract may name a
      private workspace root but must mark it reachability: operator-only, may not
      be cited as proof by any other record, and keeps personal contact details out
      of the tree.
    cost: "Two proof.status edits, a reachability: line on six records, one email moved out of core-loop.yawn."
    risk: "operator-only becomes a standing excuse and the two grandfathered sources never get vendored."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs: a record on EXTERNAL_SOURCE_GRANDFATHER may not carry proof.status: source-backed; any drive-letter value under workspace:, source_repo: or canonical_memory.root: must be followed by reachability: operator-only, and no proof.source anywhere may point at such a record's workspace."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0196"
      - "J1224"
      - "J0708"
      - "J0782"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.7
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Nothing on this axis is authored, but the reachable side has the
    proof-attached index test and the in-flight validator already implements its
    proof-block half with a shrinking ledger; the author-only side is two revealed
    observations of the same single-operator reality. The sharp violation is not
    that private paths exist but that they are graded source-backed while a real
    file in the tree is graded seed-backed (J0708): fixing the label is cheap and
    C does it. Full portability (A) needs a config mechanism the repo does not
    have and would hide the real root from inspection.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "references/july-01-lock.yawn and references/scientific-frame.yawn either vendor their sources or carry a proof.status other than source-backed, and the external-source ledger is at two by name or smaller."
    - "Every automation contract naming a drive-letter path carries reachability: operator-only and validate-proof-refs checks it."
    - "core-loop.yawn no longer carries a personal email inline."
    - "npm run validate passes with those checks present."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A new proof.source points at a private path, or source-backed survives on an
    unopenable source, and validate passes.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0196"
  - "J0353"
  - "J0710"
  - "J1224"
  - "J0708"
  - "J0782"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
